{
  title = "a node's children are one include with one identity";
  adr = "0012, 0013, 0016";
  what = "`aspect-children-bundle`: `childBundle cnf aspects [ \"loom\" ]`, written inside the tree it enumerates and included by `p` and `q`, is one node of `graphFacts`, a root, whose members are loom's walk children (the guard leaf `gate` among them). `frock` receives `gate warp weft` (the guard fired by its `rope` supplier), `smock`, reaching the bundle twice, receives each child once, and `plainHost`, reaching `loom` itself, receives loom's own content only. A host that does not reach the bundle never reads a child's throwing content, and `frock`, which does, refuses. Before, no gen export gave a node's children as one include, so every framework rebuilt the walk's membership predicate and the bundle's identity by hand.";
}
